1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,086
I'M GETTING COFFEE TO GO.
BABY DOLL?

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:04,505
I'M FINE. THANKS.

3
00:00:04,546 --> 00:00:07,007
YEAH, SEE, I CAN'T PULL OFF
"BABY DOLL," CAN I?

4
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:09,468
NO. I THINK WE LEARNED THAT FROM

5
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:10,970
THE "SUGAR LIPS" INCIDENT.

6
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,554
I'M GOING TO MAKE SOME TEA.

7
00:00:12,596 --> 00:00:14,807
HOW YOU DOING, PUNKIN'?

8
00:00:14,849 --> 00:00:17,392
NOPE.

9
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,770
IT LOOKS LIKE IT'S
GOING REALLY WELL
FOR YOU TWO, HUH?

10
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:21,104
REALLY WELL. IN FACT...

11
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:22,815
I'M GOING TO ASK PHOEBE
TO MOVE IN WITH ME.

12
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:24,149
OH, MY GOD.

13
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:25,233
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

14
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:26,360
THAT IS SO GREAT.

15
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:27,778
WHEN ARE YOU GOING
TO ASK HER?

16
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,780
TONIGHT,
BUT DON'T SAY ANYTHING, OKAY?

17
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:31,448
I SWEAR. I PROMISE,
I PROMISE.

18
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:32,658
MY GOD, I'M SO EXCITED.

19
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,409
ALL RIGHT, BUT LISTEN,
LET ME TELL YOU:

20
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,744
DO NOT GET HER
FLOWERS, OKAY?

21
00:00:35,786 --> 00:00:37,621
BECAUSE, YOU KNOW,
SHE CRIES WHEN THEY DIE

22
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:39,331
AND THEN THERE'S
THE WHOLE FUNERAL...

23
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,543
I'LL SEE YOU AFTER WORK,
SWEETIE.

24
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:44,211
OKAY. BYE.

25
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:48,632
SO, WHAT MOVIE
SHOULD WE SEE?

26
00:00:48,674 --> 00:00:50,634
GARY'S GOING TO ASK YOU
TO MOVE IN WITH HIM!

27
00:00:50,676 --> 00:00:53,846
WHAT? REALLY?

28
00:00:53,888 --> 00:00:55,263
HE JUST TOLD ME
AT THE COUNTER.

29
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:56,557
HE MADE ME PROMISE
NOT TO TELL

30
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,017
BUT I COULDN'T HOLD
IT ANY LONGER.

31
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,059
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

32
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:01,770
RIGHT, BUT BECAUSE
IT'S FAST.

33
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:03,647
BECAUSE IT'S SO FAST.
IT'S FAST.

34
00:01:03,689 --> 00:01:06,859
RELAX. IT'S PHOEBE,
NOT YOU.

35
00:01:06,901 --> 00:01:09,820
OH. GOOD FOR YOU, PHEEBS.
WAY TO GO.

36
00:01:09,862 --> 00:01:11,822
BUT IT IS FAST,
ISN'T IT?

37
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:12,990
OH...

38
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:14,950
I LIKE HIM A LOT,
BUT I'M NOT READY.

39
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:16,243
WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO?

40
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:17,912
I DON'T KNOW.
I'LL JUST HANDLE IT.

41
00:01:17,953 --> 00:01:19,329
I'LL ASK YOU TO TALK TO HIM.

42
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:22,041
ME? WHY ME?

43
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,918
BECAUSE YOU ARE SO AFRAID
OF COMMITMENT.

44
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:25,126
YOU TALK TO HIM.

45
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,461
MAKE HIM SCARED LIKE YOU.

46
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:28,005
MAKE HIM A-A MAN.

47
00:01:28,672 --> 00:01:29,965
WELL, YOU KNOW, I'LL TRY

48
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:31,216
BUT I'M NOT SURE WHAT GOOD
IT WOULD DO, YOU KNOW

49
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:33,092
BECAUSE I'M A LOT LESS AFRAID
OF COMMITMENT

50
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:34,261
THAN I USED TO BE.

51
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:36,597
OH, THAT IS SO SWEET.

52
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:37,890
STILL TERRIFIED.

53
00:01:37,932 --> 00:01:39,266
I'LL TAKE CARE OF IT.
NO PROBLEM.

54
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:42,519
( chuckling )

55
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:54,823
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

56
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:57,034
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

57
00:01:57,076 --> 00:01:59,703
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

58
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:04,625
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

59
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:06,877
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

60
00:02:06,919 --> 00:02:09,504
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

61
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:13,341
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

62
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:15,552
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

63
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:18,221
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

64
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:19,681
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

65
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:23,351
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

66
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:28,732
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

67
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:37,198
HEY, ROSS, IS, UH...

68
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,493
IS STATEN ISLAND
REALLY AN ISLAND?

69
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,869
UH-HUH.

70
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:42,871
THAT'S WHY THEY CALL IT STATEN
ISLAND.

71
00:02:42,913 --> 00:02:46,083
OH. I THOUGHT IT WAS LIKE
LONG ISLAND.

72
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:53,007
ALSO AN ISLAND.

73
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:55,634
HEY, WHAT TIME IS IT?

74
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,011
2:17.

75
00:02:57,052 --> 00:02:58,846
WOW, YOU REALIZE
WE'VE BEEN THROWING THIS BALL

76
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,555
WITHOUT DROPPING IT
FOR, LIKE, AN HOUR?

77
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:03,224
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

78
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:05,936
I REALIZED IT A HALF HOUR AGO,
BUT DIDN'T WANT TO SAY ANYTHING

79
00:03:05,978 --> 00:03:07,354
'CAUSE I DIDN'T WANT
TO JINX IT.

80
00:03:07,395 --> 00:03:08,605
OH.

81
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:10,816
WOW, WE ARE PRETTY GOOD AT THIS.

82
00:03:10,858 --> 00:03:12,400
( chuckling ):
YEAH.

83
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,402
HEY... WE TOTALLY FORGOT
ABOUT LUNCH.

84
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:17,698
OH. I THINK THAT'S THE FIRST
TIME I'VE EVER MISSED A MEAL.

85
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,074
YEAH?

86
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:21,035
YEAH. I THINK MY PANTS
ARE A LITTLE LOOSE.

87
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:27,666
HEY, YOU GUYS, UH...
IS MONICA HERE?

88
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,084
NO.
NO.
ALL RIGHT, LISTEN

89
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:30,293
I JUST BOUGHT SOMETHING.

90
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:31,712
I'M NOT SURE
SHE'S GOING TO LIKE IT

91
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,296
AND IT'S GOING TO SEEM
A LITTLE CRAZY

92
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,756
BUT THIS IS SOMETHING
I'VE WANTED

93
00:03:34,798 --> 00:03:35,924
SINCE I WAS A LITTLE GIRL.

94
00:03:35,966 --> 00:03:38,093
YOU BOUGHT SHAUN CASSIDY!

95
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:40,428
NO. I WISH.

96
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,930
OKAY... YOU READY?

97
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:43,182
YEAH.
YEAH.

98
00:03:43,222 --> 00:03:44,933
OKAY.

99
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:47,895
CHECK IT OUT.

100
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:54,068
OH, MY GOD! WHAT-WHAT IS...

101
00:03:54,109 --> 00:03:56,070
WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?

102
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:58,780
IT'S-IT'S A CAT.

103
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,281
THAT IS NOT A CAT.

104
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:02,910
YES, IT IS.

105
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:05,370
WHY IS IT INSIDE OUT?

106
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:10,625
EXCUSE ME

107
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:15,130
BUT THIS IS A PUREBRED,
SHOW-QUALITY SPHINX CAT.

108
00:04:15,172 --> 00:04:17,841
HOW MUCH DID YOU
PAY FOR THAT?

109
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:20,135
IT WAS EXTRAVAGANT,
BUT I GOT A PRETTY GOOD DEAL.

110
00:04:20,177 --> 00:04:21,386
YEAH? HOW MUCH?

111
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:22,512
A THOUSAND BUCKS.

112
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,891
ON A CAT?!

113
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,518
IT'S NOT A CAT.

114
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:30,145
WHAT...?

115
00:04:30,187 --> 00:04:31,813
ALL RIGHT, LISTEN, BALL BOYS

116
00:04:31,855 --> 00:04:34,441
MY GRANDMOTHER HAD ONE OF THESE
WHEN I WAS A LITTLE GIRL

117
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:35,943
AND IT WAS THE SWEETEST THING.

118
00:04:35,984 --> 00:04:37,444
I MEAN, IT WAS SO CUTE.

119
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:39,446
IT WOULD SIT IN MY LAP
AND JUST PURR ALL DAY LONG

120
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:41,281
AND I WOULD DRAG A SHOESTRING
ON THE GROUND

121
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,657
AND IT WOULD CHASE IT.

122
00:04:42,699 --> 00:04:44,826
FREE CATS DO THAT,
TOO, YOU KNOW.

123
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:47,495
IT'S NOT A CAT!

124
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:50,124
LOOK, YOU GUYS, I'M REALLY
EXCITED ABOUT THIS, OKAY?

125
00:04:50,165 --> 00:04:51,792
I DON'T CARE WHAT YOU THINK.

126
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:54,294
I'M GOING TO GO SET UP A
LITTER BOX FOR MRS. WHISKERSON.

127
00:04:56,379 --> 00:04:58,757
WELL, WHAT AM I GOING
TO CALL HER-- FLUFFY?

128
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,179
YOU WANT TO GET
SOMETHING TO EAT

129
00:05:04,221 --> 00:05:05,472
OR TO SEE HOW LONG

130
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:07,224
WE CAN THROW THIS BALL
BACK AND FORTH, HUH?

131
00:05:07,266 --> 00:05:09,101
UH... THE BALL THING.

132
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:10,227
YEAH?

133
00:05:10,269 --> 00:05:12,271
HEY, ROSS,
WOULDN'T IT BE GREAT

134
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:15,232
IF WE COULD GO FOR, LIKE,
TWO STRAIGHT HOURS

135
00:05:15,274 --> 00:05:16,858
WITHOUT DROPPING IT?

136
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,318
UH... YEAH, IT WOULD.

137
00:05:20,904 --> 00:05:21,863
LET'S DO IT.

138
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:23,615
OKAY.

139
00:05:26,076 --> 00:05:27,202
UH-OH.

140
00:05:27,244 --> 00:05:28,245
WHAT?

141
00:05:28,287 --> 00:05:29,579
I HAVE TO PEE

142
00:05:29,621 --> 00:05:31,957
AND RACHEL'S IN THE BATHROOM.

143
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:38,546
MAN, I DIDN'T THINK
WE WERE GOING TO MAKE IT.

144
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:41,216
I KNOW.

145
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:43,760
DON'T SWITCH HANDS, OKAY?

146
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:53,770
HEY, LADIES, WHAT ARE
YOU IN HERE FOR?

147
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:56,940
( laughs )

148
00:05:56,982 --> 00:05:59,026
HEY, CHANDLER,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

149
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,194
GARY, I AM HERE

150
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,820
TO REPORT A CRIME.

151
00:06:01,862 --> 00:06:04,656
YEAH?
IT IS A CRIME WE DON'T
SPEND MORE TIME TOGETHER.

152
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:06,241
( mock chuckle ):
WHAT'S UP?

153
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:08,535
UH, WELL, I HEARD
THAT YOU WERE THINKING ABOUT

154
00:06:08,576 --> 00:06:10,120
ASKING PHOEBE
TO MOVE IN WITH YOU

155
00:06:10,162 --> 00:06:12,164
AND I THOUGHT MAYBE
WE SHOULD HAVE A TALK

156
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:15,167
YOU KNOW, MAN-TO... WELL, ME.

157
00:06:15,209 --> 00:06:16,835
SURE. OKAY.

158
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:18,003
OKAY.

159
00:06:18,045 --> 00:06:19,921
UM, ARE YOU CRAZY?

160
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:21,673
ARE YOU INSANE?

161
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,175
IF YOU LIVE WITH PHOEBE

162
00:06:23,217 --> 00:06:25,927
YOU TWO ARE GOING TO BE
YOU KNOW, L-LIVING TOGETHER.

163
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:27,095
YEAH. I CONSIDERED THAT.

164
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:28,596
I JUST KNOW
IT'D MAKE ME HAPPY.

165
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:29,931
( laughs ):
YOU MEAN SCARED.

166
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:31,099
NO, I MEAN HAPPY.

167
00:06:31,141 --> 00:06:33,852
WELL, "SCARED HAPPY."

168
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:35,562
CHANDLER, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

169
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,356
I AM TRYING TO OPEN YOUR EYES,
MY MAN.

170
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:38,982
DON'T YOU SEE?

171
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:40,192
IF YOU LIVE WITH PHOEBE

172
00:06:40,234 --> 00:06:41,568
SHE'S ALWAYS GOING
TO BE THERE.

173
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:43,320
YOU'RE GOING TO GET
HOME-- SHE'S THERE.

174
00:06:43,362 --> 00:06:44,612
YOU GO TO BED--
SHE'S THERE.

175
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:46,489
YOU WAKE UP, AND,
OH, YES-- SHE'S THERE.

176
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:48,616
I KNOW. I CAN'T WAIT.

177
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:53,121
WERE YOUR PARENTS
HAPPY OR SOMETHING?

178
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,706
LISTEN, CHANDLER,
THE WAY I SEE IT IS

179
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:56,791
I WAS LUCKY ENOUGH TO FIND
SOMEONE I REALLY LOVE.

180
00:06:56,833 --> 00:07:00,087
I JUST... I WANT TO BE AROUND
HER AS MUCH AS I CAN.

181
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,796
WOW, YOU KNOW,
WHEN YOU SAY IT

182
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:03,382
IT DOESN'T SOUND SO SCARY.

183
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:04,883
YOU KNOW WHAT
I'M TALKING ABOUT.

184
00:07:04,925 --> 00:07:06,425
YEAH, I THINK I DO.

185
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,802
YOU KNOW WHAT?

186
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,512
YOU MOVE IN WITH HER.

187
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:11,098
YOU MOVE IN
WITH HER RIGHT NOW.

188
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:12,807
MAYBE I SHOULD MOVE
IN WITH MONICA.

189
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,393
NO, IT'S TOO SOON FOR YOU GUYS.

190
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:18,646
( chuckling ):
YOU'RE RIGHT ABOUT THAT.

191
00:07:21,358 --> 00:07:23,068
NOW, WHEN THEY
FOUND THE REMAINS

192
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:24,443
OF THE MESOZOIC MASTODON

193
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:27,114
THEY DISCOVERED
WHAT APPEARED TO BE

194
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:30,909
THE REMAINS OF A PALEOZOIC
AMPHIBIAN IN ITS JAWS.

195
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:34,162
HOW DID IT GET THERE?

196
00:07:34,204 --> 00:07:38,333
MAYBE THIS SHOULD BE
MORE OF A QUIET GAME.

197
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:41,128
HEY, GUYS.

198
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:42,421
HEY.

199
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,339
I LEFT MY WATCH
ON THE COUNTER LAST NIGHT.

200
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:45,632
IT WAS RIGHT HERE.
WHERE IS IT?

201
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:46,967
I DON'T KNOW.

202
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,676
ALL RIGHT, WELL, COME ON.
I'M LATE FOR WORK.

203
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,553
HOW DO YOU KNOW?
YOU DON'T HAVE A WATCH.

204
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:55,183
GUYS, COULD YOU PLEASE JUST STOP
THROWING THE BALL FOR ONE MINUTE

205
00:07:55,225 --> 00:07:56,351
AND JUST HELP ME FIND IT?

206
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:57,602
OH, I DON'T KNOW.

207
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:58,979
YEAH, CAN'T DO IT.

208
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,355
NO! D...

209
00:08:00,397 --> 00:08:01,398
AAH! AAH!

210
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:04,067
WHAT?

211
00:08:04,109 --> 00:08:06,694
MONICA, WHATEVER YOU DO,
DO NOT DROP THAT BALL.

212
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:08,196
YEAH. WE HAVEN'T
DROPPED IT IN...

213
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:10,365
TWO HOURS,
27 MINUTES.

214
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:14,035
REALLY?

215
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:16,330
I'M NOT GOING TO BE ABLE
TO MAKE IT INTO WORK TODAY.

216
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:18,581
( congested voice ):
UM, I DON'T FEEL VERY GOOD.

217
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:20,834
YES!

218
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:23,462
WOW, UH, FOR A SECOND THERE

219
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:25,713
I THOUGHT I WAS FEELING BETTER,
BUT I'M NOT.

220
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,757
BYE.

221
00:08:27,799 --> 00:08:28,758
Ross:
HEY, RACH.

222
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,843
HEY.

223
00:08:29,884 --> 00:08:31,219
CHECK IT OUT--

224
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:32,553
ALMOST THREE HOURS
WITHOUT DROPPING IT.

225
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,763
WHOO.

226
00:08:33,805 --> 00:08:35,390
OH, WOW. CONGRATULATIONS.

227
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:37,309
THAT'S QUITE A WASTE OF TIME.

228
00:08:39,019 --> 00:08:40,354
RACH?
YEAH?

229
00:08:40,395 --> 00:08:42,189
YOU HAVE SCRATCHES ALL OVER.
WHAT HAPPENED?

230
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,898
WELL, IT'S MY CAT.

231
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:44,732
WHAT?

232
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:45,900
OH, YEAH. I GOT A CAT.

233
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:47,152
I DON'T WANT A CAT.

234
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:48,611
OH, DON'T WORRY.
IT'S NOT A CAT.

235
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:49,821
YEAH.

236
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:51,365
YOU GUYS

237
00:08:51,406 --> 00:08:53,867
THIS CAT IS NOTHING LIKE
MY GRANDMOTHER'S CAT.

238
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:56,077
I MEAN, IT'S NOT SWEET;
IT'S NOT CUTE.

239
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,913
I EVEN DRAGGED THAT
LITTLE STRING ON THE GROUND

240
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:02,125
AND IT J-JUST FLIPPED OUT AND
SCRATCHED THE HELL OUT OF ME...

241
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:05,586
AND I SWEAR--
I KNOW THIS SOUNDS CRAZY--

242
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,714
BUT EVERY TIME
THIS CAT HISSES AT ME

243
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:08,882
I KNOW IT'S SAYING:

244
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:09,966
( whispering ):
"RACHEL."

245
00:09:16,223 --> 00:09:20,060
DOESN'T SOUND AS CRAZY
AS PAYING $1,000 FOR A CAT.

246
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:22,103
WHA...! YOU PAID
$1,000 FOR A CAT

247
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:23,688
WHEN YOU OWE ME $300?

248
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:26,607
WELL, I... I WAS GOING TO LET
YOU PLAY WITH IT.

249
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:33,240
HEY.

250
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:34,449
MM... DID YOU TALK

251
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:36,368
TO GARY
ABOUT THE MOVING IN THING?

252
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:38,245
YES, I DID, AND I THINK
YOU SHOULD DO IT.

253
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:39,746
WHAT?

254
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:42,832
HE'S A GREAT GUY, YOU KNOW,
AND HE LOVES YOU A LOT.

255
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:44,543
YOU ARE A VERY LUCKY LADY.

256
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,669
YOU ARE USELESS.

257
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:50,882
FREAKING OUT ABOUT COMMITMENT
IS THE ONE THING YOU CAN DO--

258
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,967
THE ONE THING-- AND YOU
CAN'T EVEN DO THAT RIGHT.

259
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,428
GOD.
I'M SORRY.

260
00:09:54,469 --> 00:09:56,430
IF HE ASKED ME,
I'D MOVE IN WITH HIM.

261
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:57,222
OH!

262
00:09:58,723 --> 00:10:00,016
GOD.

263
00:10:00,058 --> 00:10:01,976
OOH, GET OUT OF HERE,
YOU GOOD-FOR-NOTHING.

264
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:05,564
HEY, CHANDLER.

265
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:07,690
HEY, GAR.

266
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:10,485
HEY, SWEETIE.

267
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:12,195
HI. CAN I TALK TO YOU
FOR A SECOND?

268
00:10:12,237 --> 00:10:15,656
YEAH... 'KAY.

269
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,284
YOU LOOK VERY PRETTY TODAY.

270
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:18,785
THANKS. OKAY.

271
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:21,662
HERE'S THE THING--
YEAH?

272
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:24,583
I REALLY WANT
THIS RELATIONSHIP
TO MOVE FORWARD...
MM-HMM.

273
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,418
BECAUSE IF YOU'RE
NOT MOVING FORWARD

274
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:28,462
YOU KNOW, YOU'RE JUST
MOVING BACKWARDS.

275
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:30,046
NOW, THAT'S NOT TRUE.

276
00:10:30,088 --> 00:10:32,632
IF YOU'RE NOT MOVING FORWARD,
YOU'RE JUST STAYING STILL

277
00:10:32,673 --> 00:10:34,092
AND STAYING STILL IS GOOD.

278
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:36,094
WATCH THIS.

279
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,345
PHOEBE?

280
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:38,513
YEAH?

281
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:40,640
I WANT YOU TO
MOVE IN WITH ME.

282
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:42,850
THAT IS SO SWEET

283
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:46,020
BUT DON'T YOU THINK THAT
IT'S A LITTLE TOO SOON?

284
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:47,188
THERE'S JUST SO MUCH

285
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:48,565
THAT WE DON'T KNOW
ABOUT EACH OTHER.

286
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:51,234
OH.

287
00:10:51,276 --> 00:10:55,489
OH, OKAY, I GET IT.

288
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:57,698
I JUST... I DON'T WANT US
TO JUMP INTO SOMETHING

289
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,409
YOU KNOW, THAT WE'RE NOT...
READY FOR.

290
00:10:59,451 --> 00:11:01,495
YOU KNOW?
( trembling voice ):
UH-HUH.

291
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:05,582
I REALLY DON'T WANT
TO MESS UP WHAT WE HAVE.

292
00:11:05,624 --> 00:11:09,461
I'M JUST... I'M WORRIED IT'S
GOING TO BE A BIG MISTAKE.

293
00:11:09,503 --> 00:11:11,879
HUH.

294
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:15,925
WHICH IS WHY MY ANSWER IS YES!

295
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:17,802
REALLY?

296
00:11:17,844 --> 00:11:18,970
UH-HUH.

297
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:20,972
OH, YOU'RE SO HAPPY.

298
00:11:26,685 --> 00:11:29,397
MONICA, STOP THROWING IT
SO HARD!

299
00:11:31,149 --> 00:11:33,151
WE'RE ON THE SAME TEAM.

300
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:36,446
FOUR HOURS?

301
00:11:36,488 --> 00:11:38,114
YOU GUYS HAVE
BEEN DOING THIS
FOR FOUR HOURS?

302
00:11:38,156 --> 00:11:39,533
THAT'S RIGHT,
BABY.

303
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:40,575
ALL RIGHT, LET ME IN.

304
00:11:40,617 --> 00:11:41,660
NO, NO! DON'T DO IT!

305
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:42,827
DON'T!

306
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:44,871
WHAT?

307
00:11:44,912 --> 00:11:47,374
HE'S A DROPPER.

308
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:51,211
OH, YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT!

309
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:52,962
I'M NOT A DROPPER!

310
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:56,591
IT'S REALLY A-A-A...
THREE-PERSON GAME, YOU KNOW?

311
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:59,718
IT'S THROWING AND CATCHING.

312
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,804
ALL RIGHT.

313
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:06,976
OH, OH, IT'S SO HARD.

314
00:12:14,568 --> 00:12:17,111
DON'T WORRY, GUYS.
IT'S NOT A CAT.

315
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:21,658
OH, MY...
OH, GOOD GOD.

316
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,201
I GIVE UP, YOU GUYS.

317
00:12:23,243 --> 00:12:25,579
I DON'T KNOW WHAT
I'M GOING TO DO WITH THIS THING.

318
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,746
BAKING IT DIDN'T HELP, HUH?

319
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:30,458
SO WHY DON'T YOU

320
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,711
JUST TAKE IT BACK
TO WHERE YOU GOT IT?

321
00:12:32,751 --> 00:12:34,795
I TRIED.
THEY WON'T TAKE HER BACK.

322
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:39,175
MAYBE THAT'S BECAUSE SHE'S
A MINION OF THE ANTI-CHRIST.

323
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:41,261
RACH...

324
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:42,470
WHY WON'T THEY
TAKE IT BACK?

325
00:12:42,512 --> 00:12:43,888
WELL, THEY SAID THEY WOULD

326
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,682
BUT THEY WOULD ONLY GIVE ME
STORE CREDIT

327
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:47,267
AND, I MEAN,
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO?

328
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:48,767
GET A THOUSAND REGULAR CATS?

329
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:50,103
YOU CAN KEEP IT
AT OUR PLACE

330
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,938
UNTIL YOU FIND OUT
WHAT TO DO WITH IT.

331
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:53,940
NO, MON, THAT'S NOT THE POINT.

332
00:12:53,981 --> 00:12:56,401
I AM OUT $1,000;
I AM ALL SCRATCHED UP

333
00:12:56,443 --> 00:12:59,862
AND I'M STUCK WITH THIS STUPID
CAT THAT LOOKS LIKE A HAND.

334
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,658
( sneezes )

335
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,159
OH, MY GOD.

336
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,703
THE CAT'S MADE
MY EYES WATER.

337
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:08,162
DON'T-DON'T
THROW IT TO ME!

338
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:11,082
MY VISION'S
BEEN COMPROMISED!

339
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:14,628
OH, GOD. OKAY, OKAY...

340
00:13:14,669 --> 00:13:16,755
IT'S OKAY.

341
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:18,089
MAN, THAT WAS CLOSE.

342
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:21,551
YEAH. YOU ALMOST OVERREACTED
TO SOMETHING.

343
00:13:21,593 --> 00:13:22,969
HEY.
HEY.

344
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:23,970
HEY.
HEY.

345
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:25,138
WE HAVE GREAT NEWS.

346
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:26,640
WE'RE MOVING IN TOGETHER!

347
00:13:26,681 --> 00:13:27,890
ISN'T IT GREAT? YAY!

348
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:29,309
YAY!

349
00:13:29,350 --> 00:13:30,809
CONGRATULATIONS.
THAT'S GREAT.

350
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,103
I KNOW. I'M SO EXCITED.

351
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:33,480
SO AM I.

352
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:35,148
WELL, YOU'RE NOT
MORE EXCITED THAN I AM.

353
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,441
NO WAY.
I'M THE MOST EXCITED.

354
00:13:36,483 --> 00:13:38,443
OKAY, I'LL SEE YOU
AT THE STATION LATER.

355
00:13:38,485 --> 00:13:39,778
YEAH, I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

356
00:13:39,818 --> 00:13:41,738
DON'T FORGET
ABOUT THE MOVING IN.

357
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,030
ALL RIGHT.

358
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,949
YOU'RE MOVING IN WITH
HIM? WHAT HAPPENED?

359
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:47,285
I COULDN'T TELL HIM NO--
HE GOT SO SAD.

360
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:49,120
BUT MAYBE IT'LL BE ALL RIGHT.

361
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:50,829
I DO REALLY
LIKE HIM A LOT

362
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:53,832
AND WOULD PROBABLY DO IT
EVENTUALLY ANYWAY...

363
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:57,044
AND, PLUS, THINK OF ALL
THE MONEY I'LL SAVE ON STAMPS.

364
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:59,464
WHY, DO YOU
WRITE HIM A LOT?

365
00:13:59,506 --> 00:14:01,882
NO. I JUST HEARD
WHEN PEOPLE LIVE TOGETHER

366
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:04,427
THEY SPLIT THE COST OF STAMPS,
DON'T THEY?

367
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:07,639
YEAH.

368
00:14:07,681 --> 00:14:09,140
THAT'S RIGHT. YEAH, YEAH.

369
00:14:10,642 --> 00:14:11,934
OH!

370
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,144
OH... I'M SORRY.

371
00:14:13,186 --> 00:14:15,563
THE OVEN MITTS
REALLY FREAKED ME OUT.

372
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:24,364
HI, HONEY.
HEY, HONEY.

373
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:27,867
DID YOU FIND ANY APARTMENTS
IN BROOKLYN HEIGHTS?

374
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,243
NO. NOTHING.

375
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:30,244
OH. REALLY?

376
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,245
YEAH.

377
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:32,706
NOTHING AT ALL?
NO.

378
00:14:32,747 --> 00:14:34,541
AS SOON AS SOMETHING OPENS UP,
WE'LL MOVE RIGHT IN.

379
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,584
UNLESS IT DOESN'T HAVE A POOL;
I NEED A POOL.

380
00:14:38,503 --> 00:14:40,505
PHOEBE, CAN I TALK
TO YOU FOR A SECOND?

381
00:14:40,547 --> 00:14:42,465
UH-HUH.

382
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,218
TAKE A SEAT.

383
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:47,053
ALL RIGHT.

384
00:14:47,094 --> 00:14:48,388
YOU OKAY?

385
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:50,973
YOU FEELING
ALL RIGHT?

386
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:53,892
YEAH, I FEEL GREAT,
'CAUSE WE'RE MOVING IN TOGETHER.

387
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:55,603
SO YOU, UH...

388
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,938
YOU CHECKED THE PAPER
FOR LISTINGS

389
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,774
IN BROOKLYN
HEIGHTS, RIGHT?

390
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,819
YOU-YOU CHECKED THE POST?

391
00:15:02,861 --> 00:15:05,613
YEAH. UH-HUH. THERE WAS NOTHING.

392
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,324
COULD I GET SOME WATER?

393
00:15:08,366 --> 00:15:11,411
IN A MINUTE.

394
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:12,995
YOU-YOU CHECKED TODAY'S POST?

395
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:14,914
UM, YEAH. TODAY'S. MM-HMM.

396
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:16,123
HMM...

397
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:18,710
'CAUSE, UH, THIS
IS TODAY'S POST

398
00:15:18,752 --> 00:15:21,379
AND, UH, THESE ARE
THE LISTINGS I FOUND.

399
00:15:21,421 --> 00:15:23,381
"BROOKLYN HEIGHTS,
TWO BEDROOMS."

400
00:15:23,423 --> 00:15:25,341
"BROOKLYN HEIGHTS,
ONE BEDROOM."

401
00:15:25,383 --> 00:15:28,762
"BROOKLYN HEIGHTS," "BROOKLYN
HEIGHTS," "BROOKLYN HEIGHTS."

402
00:15:28,803 --> 00:15:30,263
OH, ARE THESE FOR RENT?

403
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,640
I THOUGHT PEOPLE
WERE JUST BRAGGING.

404
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:36,644
LET ME TELL YOU WHAT I THINK
MIGHT BE GOING ON HERE.

405
00:15:36,686 --> 00:15:38,104
NO, NO. DON'T
LOOK AT THE TABLE.

406
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:38,938
LOOK AT ME.

407
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,981
OKAY?

408
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:43,443
I THINK SOMEBODY ASKED SOMEONE
TO MOVE IN WITH HIM

409
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:44,903
AND I THINK SOMEONE SAID YES

410
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,571
BUT NOW SHE'S HAVING
DOUBTS 'CAUSE

411
00:15:46,613 --> 00:15:48,948
MAYBE THINGS ARE MOVING TOO FAST
FOR SOMEONE.

412
00:15:48,989 --> 00:15:50,157
DOES THAT SOUND AT ALL

413
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,492
POSSIBLE TO YOU?

414
00:15:51,534 --> 00:15:53,703
YES, YES, YES, FINE!

415
00:15:53,745 --> 00:15:56,414
I AM SOMEONE!

416
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:57,957
YOU WANT ME TO SAY IT?

417
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:59,292
I HAVE DOUBTS.

418
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:02,754
I'M SORRY!

419
00:16:02,796 --> 00:16:04,004
PHOEBE?

420
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:05,298
YEAH?

421
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:07,467
PHOEBE, IT'S OKAY
THAT YOU FEEL THIS WAY.

422
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:09,302
I MEAN, IT IS SOON

423
00:16:09,343 --> 00:16:11,554
AND THERE'S A LOT OF THINGS
WE DON'T KNOW ABOUT EACH OTHER.

424
00:16:11,596 --> 00:16:14,390
I FIGURED EVERYTHING I KNOW
ABOUT YOU, I REALLY LIKE;

425
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:16,643
AND THE THINGS I DON'T KNOW,
I'D GET TO LEARN ABOUT

426
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:18,812
IN A PLACE WITH BOTH OUR
NAMES ON THE MAILBOX.

427
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:21,230
THAT'S SO SWEET.

428
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:22,690
SWEETHEART

429
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:25,151
BUT NONE OF THAT MATTERS
IF IT'S TOO SOON FOR YOU.

430
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:27,487
IT'S FINE. WE DON'T HAVE
TO MOVE IN TOGETHER.

431
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:29,155
I JUST... I WANT
YOU TO BE HAPPY.

432
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:31,616
LIVING WITH YOU
WOULD MAKE ME HAPPY.

433
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:33,033
YOU DON'T HAVE TO SAY THAT.

434
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,702
NO, I REALLY WANT
TO LIVE WITH YOU.

435
00:16:34,744 --> 00:16:36,078
I WANT TO MOVE IN WITH YOU.

436
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,497
ARE YOU SURE?

437
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:39,499
YES. DEFINITELY, YES.

438
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:42,001
LET'S LIVE IN AN APARTMENT
THAT WE BOTH LIVE IN.

439
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:43,503
OH, THAT'S GREAT!

440
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:45,212
OH, WAIT.
ONE SEC, ONE SEC.

441
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:49,300
HEY, YOU-- BEHIND THE GLASS--
WHO ARE YOU LOOKING AT?!

442
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:50,718
I'VE ALWAYS WANTED TO SAY THAT

443
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:52,553
EVERY TIME I WAS
IN ONE OF THESE ROOMS

444
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:54,012
WHICH WAS NEVER.

445
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:59,017
Rachel:
SHOW CAT!

446
00:16:59,059 --> 00:17:02,480
QUALITY SHOW CAT!

447
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:03,857
SHOW CAT!

448
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:05,023
OH, MY GOD!

449
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:07,360
WHAT'S WRONG
WITH YOUR BABY?

450
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:08,528
NO, THAT'S NOT A BABY.

451
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:09,779
THAT'S A CAT.

452
00:17:09,821 --> 00:17:11,197
EWW, IT'S CREEPY LOOKING.

453
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,782
OH, NO.

454
00:17:12,824 --> 00:17:14,158
ACTUALLY, IT'S VERY SWEET.

455
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,326
IT'S VERY SWEET. LOOK.

456
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:16,577
( vicious hissing )

457
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,623
YEAH. DO YOU WANT IT?

458
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:21,875
( chuckling )

459
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:23,501
NO. I HATE CATS.

460
00:17:23,543 --> 00:17:26,128
WELL, SO, THEN WHAT ARE
YOU DOING TO ME? OKAY?

461
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,506
JUST GET OUT OF HERE,
ALL RIGHT? MOVE ON.

462
00:17:28,548 --> 00:17:30,383
SHEESH.

463
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,092
WOW, WHAT AN UNUSUAL CAT.

464
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,553
YES. THANK YOU. EXACTLY.

465
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:34,721
YOU WANT IT?

466
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,180
MAYBE.

467
00:17:36,222 --> 00:17:37,724
I WAS THINKING
ABOUT GETTING A CAT.

468
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:39,767
I WAS JUST GOING TO GO
TO THE SHELTER, BUT...

469
00:17:39,809 --> 00:17:41,143
OKAY, WHY NOT?

470
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,228
OH, TERRIFIC.

471
00:17:42,269 --> 00:17:43,521
THAT'LL BE $2,000.

472
00:17:43,563 --> 00:17:45,398
WHAT?

473
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:46,691
OKAY, $1,000.

474
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:48,568
I THOUGHT YOU WANTED ME
TO ADOPT YOUR CAT.

475
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,110
WELL, I DO

476
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:52,405
BUT YOU'RE JUST GOING TO HAVE
TO ACTUALLY LOOK AT THIS

477
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:54,072
AS MORE OF AN INVESTMENT
THAN A CAT.

478
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:56,116
OKAY, YEAH.
I JUST WANTED A CAT.

479
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,451
YEAH. OKAY, OKAY...

480
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:59,119
( stammering )

481
00:17:59,161 --> 00:18:01,247
OBVIOUSLY, YOU KNOW
HOW TO HAGGLE

482
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:04,208
SO I'M NOT GOING TO TRY
AND TAKE YOU ON, OKAY?

483
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:07,211
SO $800 AND I DON'T CALL
THE COPS, WHICH I SHOULD

484
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:09,672
BECAUSE YOU ARE
ROBBING ME BLIND! BLIND!

485
00:18:09,714 --> 00:18:12,258
JUST TAKE THE CAT, LEAVE
THE MONEY AND RUN AWAY.

486
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:13,467
JUST RUN AWAY.

487
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:14,844
DAMN IT!

488
00:18:14,886 --> 00:18:17,764
CAN'T YOU AT LEAST SMILE
OR SOMETHING?

489
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,473
( vicious hissing )

490
00:18:20,850 --> 00:18:22,685
OKAY, DID ANYBODY
JUST HEAR THAT?

491
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:23,937
ANYBODY?

492
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:32,110
I'M STARVING.

493
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,905
COME ON, GUYS,
SUCK IT UP.

494
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:35,782
WE'RE CLOSING IN ON TEN HOURS.

495
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:38,117
IT'S GUT-CHECK TIME.

496
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:40,286
I DON'T KNOW WHO MADE YOU
THE BOSS, ALL RIGHT?

497
00:18:40,327 --> 00:18:41,454
WE INVENTED THIS GAME.

498
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:42,496
Monica:
PLEASE.

499
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:44,707
I MADE THIS GAME WHAT IT IS.

500
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:46,793
NOT FUN ANYMORE?

501
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:49,462
I'M STILL HUNGRY.

502
00:18:49,503 --> 00:18:50,713
THERE'S PIZZA
AT MY PLACE.

503
00:18:50,755 --> 00:18:52,298
WE CAN ALL EAT
WITH ONE HAND, RIGHT?

504
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,466
ARE YOU WITH ME?

505
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:54,842
I AM.

506
00:18:54,884 --> 00:18:57,011
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO!
COME ON! COME ON!

507
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:58,471
LET'S GO, TEAM MONICA!

508
00:19:01,307 --> 00:19:03,059
WE CAN WORK OUT
THAT NAME LATER.

509
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,480
RACHEL...

510
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,774
WHAT IS YOUR CAT DOING
IN ONE OF MY BOWLS?

511
00:19:09,816 --> 00:19:11,609
IT'S NOT.
I'M DEFROSTING A CHICKEN.

512
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:15,905
OH, I SOLD MRS. WHISKERSON.

513
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:17,740
OH, THANK GOD.

514
00:19:17,782 --> 00:19:19,075
DID YOU GET YOUR MONEY BACK?

515
00:19:19,117 --> 00:19:20,534
YEAH. $1,500.

516
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,541
I JUST CAME
FOR THE RED VELVET PILLOW.

517
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:28,876
OH, YEAH.

518
00:19:28,918 --> 00:19:31,045
THERE YOU GO.

519
00:19:31,087 --> 00:19:33,047
THANKS, RACHEL,
AND, UH, DON'T FORGET

520
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:35,215
YOU CAN COME VISIT HER
ANYTIME YOU WANT.

521
00:19:35,257 --> 00:19:36,425
OH, GOOD. GREAT.

522
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:37,885
I-I'LL KEEP THAT IN MIND.

523
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:42,556
HEY.

524
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:45,893
SO WHAT IS THIS, SOME KIND
OF SNAKE OR SOMETHING?

525
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:55,235
( bird chirping )

526
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:58,531
I REALLY LIKE WAKING UP
WITH YOU.

527
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,908
I LIKE WAKING UP
WITH YOU, TOO.

528
00:20:00,950 --> 00:20:03,161
OH, IT'S SUCH
A BEAUTIFUL MORNING.

529
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:06,122
I COULD STAY HERE ALL DAY.

530
00:20:06,164 --> 00:20:07,623
THAT WOULD BE GREAT.

531
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:09,750
WE COULD HAVE
BREAKFAST IN BED...

532
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:11,418
WELL, JUST A SECOND.

533
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:12,586
OKAY.

534
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:14,338
OH!
( chirping stops )

535
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,549
OH, NO.

536
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:21,012
ALL RIGHT,
COME ON, MONICA!

537
00:20:21,054 --> 00:20:22,180
LOOK ALIVE.

538
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:23,389
COME ON, LOOK ALIVE.

539
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:29,687
OH, GOOD, YOU'RE ALL UP.

540
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:30,813
HEY.
HEY.

541
00:20:30,855 --> 00:20:32,190
PHOEBE, IT'S 6:00
IN THE MORNING.

542
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,399
WHY AREN'T YOU
AT GARY'S?

543
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:35,275
OH, YEAH. THAT'S OVER.
WHAT?
WHAT?

544
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:36,777
GARY'S SUCH A GREAT GUY.

545
00:20:36,819 --> 00:20:38,487
WHATEVER THE PROBLEM IS,
YOU CAN WORK IT OUT.

546
00:20:38,529 --> 00:20:39,279
HE SHOT A BIRD.

547
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,656
OH, THAT IS OVER.

548
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:42,992
Rachel:
OH, HONEY,
I'M SORRY.

549
00:20:43,034 --> 00:20:44,035
THAT'S TERRIBLE.

550
00:20:44,077 --> 00:20:45,161
PHOEBE, ARE YOU OKAY?

551
00:20:45,203 --> 00:20:47,413
YEAH, YEAH, I'LL BE ALL RIGHT.

552
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:49,123
WELL, HEY,
HERE, PHEEBS.

553
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:51,333
OH. NAH, I DON'T FEEL
LIKE PLAYING.

554
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:52,877
( collective gasp )

555
00:20:56,047 --> 00:20:57,506
IT'S OKAY.

556
00:20:57,548 --> 00:20:59,258
IT'S OKAY, OKAY?

557
00:20:59,299 --> 00:21:01,177
LOOK...

558
00:21:01,219 --> 00:21:03,012
JUST PRETEND THAT
IT DIDN'T HAPPEN, OKAY?

559
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:04,388
NO ONE NEEDS TO KNOW.

560
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:06,306
PHOEBE... PHOEBE'S NOT
AN OFFICIAL BALLPLAYER.

561
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:08,768
I MEAN, ONLY OFFICIAL
BALLPLAYERS CAN DROP THE BALL.

562
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,187
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO.
OKAY.

563
00:21:11,229 --> 00:21:12,646
Rachel:
OKAY.

564
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:14,356
PHOEBE, WANT TO GET
SOME BREAKFAST?

565
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:15,357
YEAH.
OKAY.

566
00:21:15,399 --> 00:21:16,442
OKAY, LET'S RACE.

567
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:17,818
FIRST ONE THERE WINS.

568
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:19,987
HA-HA!

569
00:21:20,029 --> 00:21:21,572
YOU GUYS WANT
TO EAT HERE?

570
00:21:21,614 --> 00:21:22,907
YEAH.
YEAH.
YEAH.

571
00:21:28,913 --> 00:21:30,497
OH, MAN, THAT
WAS GREAT, HUH?

572
00:21:30,539 --> 00:21:31,540
CAN YOU BELIEVE HOW LONG

573
00:21:31,582 --> 00:21:33,000
WE THREW THAT BALL AROUND?

574
00:21:33,042 --> 00:21:35,044
I KNOW. IT IS AMAZING
IT LASTED THAT LONG.

575
00:21:35,086 --> 00:21:36,629
I KNOW. MY ARM
IS KILLING ME.

576
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:38,798
NO. I MEANT WITH THE DROPPER
OVER HERE.

577
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,424
Ross:
OH, YEAH.

578
00:21:40,466 --> 00:21:42,802
HOW DID I GET THIS REPUTATION
AS A DROPPER, OKAY?

579
00:21:42,843 --> 00:21:44,804
I'M ANYTHING BUT A DROPPER.

580
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,597
ROSS.

581
00:21:54,605 --> 00:21:57,608
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

